@BulletDescGeneric(ARGS)
#FUNCTIONS
SELECTCASE ARGS
CASE "espkill"
RETURNF "Gensou-chan ESPKill bullets are a range of bullets that deal damage according to what element they are blessed with. These have been proven to be effective against natural youkai armor as well as conventional protection as well. They use Yojipowder, raw Youjutsu essence turned into a very powerful propellent."
CASE "espkill-arrow"
RETURNF "Gensou-chan ESPKill arrows are a range of arrows that deal damage according to what element they are blessed with. These have been proven to be effective against natural youkai armor as well as conventional protection as well. They use Yojipowder, raw Youjutsu essence turned into a very powerful propellent, to propell the arrow as its being fired from the bow."
CASE "espkill-psi"
RETURNF " While ESPKill-Psi primarily damages the mind, firearms with ESPKill are still banned in Spell Card restricted Danmaku due to them still being lethal."
CASE "espkill-zan"
RETURNF "ESPKill-Zan is designed to be a high-explosive anti-personal cartridge, dealing its force damage within the explosion. The armor piercing penetrator goes through the conventional ballistic protection and then explodes within the target's body, doing devistating damage. The high-explosive is not an explosive per-say, but rather a cast of Zan, hence the name."
CASE "espkill-agi"
RETURNF "Being an incinderary cartridge, ESPKill-Agi deals fire damage and has a chance of causing burns."
CASE "espkill-bufu"
RETURNF "Bufu is a super-chilled cartridge, designed to cause frostbite burns when hit. Typically gunshots create heat, but the ESP-Bufu bullet causes hit parts to get cooler, not hotter."
CASE "espkill-frei"
RETURNF "ESPKill-Frei uses a radioactive uranium penetrator to deal radioactive damage."
CASE "espkill-dorima"
RETURNF "Designed to be non-lethal in nature, ESPKill-Dorima knocks the target out of the battle, neutralizing the enemy safely and for longer than typical solutions. It can be used as a short-term knockout, or used repeatedly to make the target unconscious due to running out of stamina."
CASE "luninco-youkai"
RETURNF "A copy of Gensou-chan's ESPKill bullets, with only the Psychosis-damaging aspect remining. Overpressured variant."
CASE "simunition"
RETURNF "round tip cartridge with a 1 gram hollow PLA plastic bullet, intended for less lethal and Force-On-Force deployment (hence F2F). Powered by only it's primer, it's meant to incapacitate, not kill."
CASE "gpt"
RETURNF "Ground Protection Tops are the Federation's primary protection against damage to its infantry."
CASE "pissAmmo"
RETURNF ", dipped in the urine of various animals, including humans and Youkai, the bullet penetrates the armor and skin with its full-metal jacket bullet, then using the open wound as a vector to spread the bacteria, attempts to infect the wound. This process deals Decay damage and is best suited against \"pure\" beings such as Lunarians."
CASE "youpan"
RETURNF "Youpan from Keiga Enterprises are panties with a little magical secret. Youpan use Youjutsu energy from your excretions to cast spells. To cast a spell, just pee or poop inside of them. If you need to go, just push a load and watch the magic do it's thing. The bigger the mess, the stronger the spell. If its already leaking or blowing out, it won't cast until it's cleaned off."
CASE "emag"
RETURNF "E-MAG, short for Esper-Maximum Absorbency Garment brings a new tactical way to cast Esper moves, while also making combining the absorbency of the MAG. E-MAG uses your leakage to power itself and cast spells for you. The more you leak in one accident, the stronger the spell that will be casted. Changing between E-MAGs is easy with its belted design and with superabsorbent material that holds 3 full bladder and 2 full bowel accidents as well as leak barriers, E-MAG makes diapers a must-have for adventurers."
CASE "brim"
RETURNF "Need magic fast? Wish you could fight back against Coprodyne spammers? Grab a BRIM, short for Blort-Reaction Instant Magic. These will cast a spell related to how the garment is attuned when soiled with either pee or poop. The amount of mess you pack inside determines what spell is cast, and it'll keep allowing you to cast until it leaks or blows out."
CASE "brim-agi"
RETURNF "Agi-attuned underwear casts single-target fire spells such as Agi, Agilao, and Agidyne on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-bufu"
RETURNF "Bufu-attuned underwear casts single-target ice spells such as Bufu, Bufula, and Bufudyne on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-dia"
RETURNF "Dia-attuned underwear casts single-target healing spells such as Dia, Diarama, and Diarahan on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-psi"
RETURNF "Psi-attuned underwear casts single-target psychic spells such as Psi, Psio, and Psiodyne on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-frei"
RETURNF "Frei-attuned underwear casts single-target radiation spells such as Frei, Freila, and Freidyne on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-zan"
RETURNF "Zan-attuned underwear casts single-target force spells such as Zan, Zanma, and Zandyne on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants."
CASE "brim-tarakaja"
RETURNF "Tarukaja-attuned underwear casts Tarukaja on wetting. Pooping in them cast multi-target variants. More servere soiling can cast better variants."
CASE "brim-fb"
RETURNF "BRIM-FB is a variant of the FantastaBab diaper, complete with its features such as its thick superabsorbent core, stay-dry Vivi coating, thick plastic backing, standing leak guards, four refastenabe tapes, wetness indicator, and more."
CASE "brim-dd"
RETURNF "With BRIM-DD, you combine Youjutsu magic with the ultimate absorbency of the Dai-diaper, complete with its melting-cute random Touhou print. The extra padding compared to the FB also announces it's presence to the user, making them have to waddle around everywhere. Not like that's a bad thing."
CASE "brim-fbp"
RETURNF "The FantastaBab+ variant known as the FBP has third generation superabsorbents that allows the FBP to absorb an extreme amount of pee and the stretchy platic backing and super tall leak guards that are great at keeping loads of poop in. With the FBP, you'll be safe that your messiest loads will bloom into awesome spells that shift the fight to your advantage."
CASE "brim-ddp"
RETURNF "A Dai-diaper+ enhanced with Youjutsu, the BRIM-DDP is a hyper diaper like no other. When dry, it pops out of even a knee-length skirt which onesies can't even cover for. When soiled, it turns into a dreamy bean bag of wetness and mess. Like the regular Dai-diaper+, it comes with a stretchy plastic backing, super tall leak guards, infectiously adorable character prints, a wetness indicator, super comfy waistbands, and refastenable tapes."
CASE "brim-pu"
RETURNF @"Like a FantastaBab in a pull-up form, the BRIM-PU are thick pull-ups with a thick core, elastic wasitband, and the Gensou-chan signature character prints. They can certainly be pulled down, but it's assumed that whoever's wearing them is going to be peeing \@ nScat ? %"and pooping "% #\@in their pants regularly."
CASEELSE
ENDSELECT

@DD17Hit(ARG,ARG:1)
#DIM nChance
nChance = 30 - (10*DamageResist:(ARG):(7):1)

IF RAND(100) <= nChance
    ;lose their turn
    SETCOLOR C_RED
    CALL LC_PRINT(@"%CALLNAME:ARG% was shocked and lost their turn!", , 2,)
    RESETCOLOR
    DT_CELL_SET "lcCombatants", GetCombatant(ARG), "didAttack", 2, 1
ENDIF

@ArousalBulletHit(ARG,ARG:1)
CFLAG:ARG:溜まってる度 += 300
SETCOLOR C_YELLOW
CALL LC_PRINT(@"%CALLNAME:ARG% starts to feel a little more flustered.", , 2,)
RESETCOLOR

